@startuml sd_snapshot_startup
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
title Scenario: a replica fills its copy of another service's data on startup (snapshot)

autonumber
participant "flight-ops-2\n(starting)" as fo
database "its read model" as rm
queue "RabbitMQ" as mq
participant "aircraft-maintenance\n(any replica)" as am
database "its read model" as amrm

fo -> mq : declare its queue, bound to aircraft.*\n(events from now on wait there)
fo -> mq : command snapshot {entity: aircraft} (reply-to)
mq -> am : one replica takes it
am -> amrm : every row of aircraft, deleted ones too, with their stamps
am --> fo : the rows
fo -> rm : apply each row if later (same rule as the events)
fo -> fo : ready (readiness probe)
note over fo, am
  Events received meanwhile and the snapshot can arrive in any order: the stamp decides.
  No answer, or an empty one: asked again every 15 s; then every 5 minutes as a check.
end note
@enduml
